---
// src/pages/en/projects/circon.astro
import BaseLayout from "../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import TextFadeIn from "../../../components/TextFadeIn.astro";

const frontmatter = {
  title: "Project Circon - Advanced Data Visualization Platform",
  navTitle: "Project Circon",
  description:
    "An in-depth look at Project Circon, a platform designed for real-time data analysis and visualization, helping businesses make informed decisions.",
  publishDate: "2024-05-08",
  heroImage: "/images/projects/circon-hero.jpg", // Ensure this path is correct
  tags: [
    "Data Visualization",
    "Real-time Analytics",
    "SaaS",
    "Platform Development",
  ],
};
---

<BaseLayout title={frontmatter.title} description={frontmatter.description}>
  <article class="project-detail-page prose dark:prose-invert prose-lg lg:prose-xl mx-auto px-4 py-8">
    {
      frontmatter.heroImage && (
        <div class="hero-image-container mb-8 not-prose">
          <img
            src={frontmatter.heroImage}
            alt={`${frontmatter.title} hero image`}
            class="w-full rounded-lg shadow-lg object-cover"
            style="max-height: 60vh; height: auto; aspect-ratio: 16/9;" /* Adjust max-height and aspect-ratio as needed */
            loading="lazy"
          />
        </div>
      )
    }

    <TextFadeIn targetSelectors="h1" blockStaggerDelay={0} baseDelay={50} wordDelay={35}>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold mb-4 text-center md:text-left !leading-tight">
        {frontmatter.title}
      </h1>
    </TextFadeIn>

    <div
      class="project-meta text-center md:text-left mb-8 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 text-sm"
    >
      {
        frontmatter.publishDate && (
          <time datetime={frontmatter.publishDate} class="block md:inline mb-2 md:mb-0 md:mr-4">
            Published:{" "}
            {new Date(frontmatter.publishDate).toLocaleDateString("en-US", {
              year: "numeric",
              month: "long",
              day: "numeric",
            })}
          </time>
        )
      }
      {
        frontmatter.tags && frontmatter.tags.length > 0 && (
          <div class="tags mt-2 md:mt-0 md:inline">
            <strong class="hidden md:inline">Tags:</strong>
            {frontmatter.tags.map((tag) => (
              <span class="tag inline-block bg-slate-200 dark:bg-slate-700 rounded-full px-3 py-1 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-200 mr-2 mb-2">
                #{tag}
              </span>
            ))}
          </div>
        )
      }
    </div>

    <TextFadeIn targetSelectors="h2, h3, p, li" baseDelay={20} wordDelay={20} blockStaggerDelay={100}>
      <section class="content-section mb-10">
        <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-semibold mb-4">Project Overview</h2>
        <p>
          Project Circon is a cutting-edge platform developed to address the
          growing need for intuitive and powerful real-time data visualization
          and analytics. In an era where data is king, Circon empowers
          businesses to unlock insights from complex datasets through an
          accessible and highly customizable interface.
        </p>
        <p>
          The core mission was to build a scalable, performant, and
          user-friendly tool that could integrate seamlessly with various data
          sources and provide actionable intelligence at a glance.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="content-section mb-10">
        <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-semibold mb-4">Key Features</h2>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-3">
          <li>
            <strong>Real-time Dashboarding:</strong> Dynamic dashboards that update
            instantaneously with incoming data streams.
          </li>
          {/* ... other list items ... */}
           <li>
            <strong>Interactive Charts & Graphs:</strong> A rich library of customizable
            charts (bar, line, pie, scatter, heatmaps, etc.) with drill-down capabilities.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Multi-Source Data Integration:</strong> Connectors for popular
            databases, APIs, and cloud services.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Advanced Filtering & Segmentation:</strong> Tools to easily slice
            and dice data for granular analysis.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Alerting & Notifications:</strong> Customizable alerts based
            on predefined thresholds or anomalous patterns.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Collaborative Workspaces:</strong> Share dashboards and insights
            with team members securely.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Responsive Design:</strong> Fully accessible on desktops, tablets,
            and mobile devices.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="content-section mb-10">
        <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-semibold mb-4">Technologies Used</h2>
        <p>
          The platform was built using a modern technology stack, focusing on
          performance, scalability, and developer experience:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2">
          <li>
            <strong>Frontend:</strong> React, TypeScript, D3.js (for custom visualizations),
            Tailwind CSS
          </li>
          {/* ... other list items ... */}
          <li>
            <strong>Backend:</strong> Node.js with Express.js, Python (for data processing
            microservices)
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Database:</strong> PostgreSQL, Redis (for caching and session
            management)
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Infrastructure:</strong> Docker, Kubernetes, AWS (EC2, S3, RDS)
          </li>
          <li><strong>Real-time Communication:</strong> WebSockets</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="content-section mb-10">
        <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-semibold mb-4">Challenges & Solutions</h2>
        <p>
          One of the primary challenges was handling high-velocity data streams
          and rendering complex visualizations without performance degradation.
          This was addressed by implementing efficient data aggregation
          techniques on the backend, optimizing frontend rendering with
          virtualized lists and memoization, and leveraging WebAssembly for
          computationally intensive tasks.
        </p>
        <p>
          Ensuring data security and compliance was another critical aspect, met
          by robust authentication mechanisms, role-based access control, and
          end-to-end encryption.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="content-section mb-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-semibold mb-4">Project Outcome</h2>
        <p>
          Project Circon successfully launched and has been adopted by several
          pilot companies, receiving positive feedback for its performance and
          ease of use. It has enabled users to gain deeper insights into their
          operations, leading to improved efficiency and data-driven
          decision-making.
        </p>
      </section>
    </TextFadeIn>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  /* Scoped styles for the project page */
  .project-detail-page {
    /* font-family: var(--font-sans); /* Inherited */
  }

  .hero-image-container img {
    /* The class="w-full" handles width: 100%; */
    /* The inline style="max-height: 60vh; height: auto; aspect-ratio: 16/9;" handles responsiveness */
    /* You can adjust 60vh (60% of viewport height) and aspect-ratio (e.g., 16/9, 4/3, 21/9) to your preference */
  }
</style>
